1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:01,990
Here you go, Lola Maxi, looking great!

2
00:00:02,028 --> 00:00:04,456
Tash! Andres!

3
00:00:07,198 --> 00:00:08,198
Are you guys ready?

4
00:00:08,227 --> 00:00:08,700
Wow!

5
00:00:08,725 --> 00:00:12,688
- We've been ready for a while!
- Of course, we've been ready for ages!

6
00:00:12,713 --> 00:00:14,108
- Perfect!
- Wait, wait, wait, hold on!

7
00:00:14,132 --> 00:00:14,716
What?

8
00:00:14,741 --> 00:00:17,473
Before we go out, I
just want to say, guys –

9
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:20,253
congrats to us!

10
00:00:22,707 --> 00:00:23,615
Hey, but wait –

11
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:29,247
congrats to you too, for all your hard
work and coming up with new ideas.

12
00:00:29,272 --> 00:00:30,402
- That’s right!
- Thank you!

13
00:00:30,427 --> 00:00:31,427
Your mom’s right.

14
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:36,272
You know, Atasha, Andres, I just
want to look you both in the eye –.

15
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:42,484
I want to thank you for
all your sacrifices for us.

16
00:00:42,632 --> 00:00:43,620
Thank you!

17
00:00:43,645 --> 00:00:50,183
Thank you so much for the time
you give your mom, Lola Maxi, and me.

18
00:00:50,728 --> 00:00:52,128
- Awww...
- I love you both so much.

19
00:00:52,153 --> 00:00:54,617
- Thank you, thank you so much.
- Awww, thanks, Dad!

20
00:00:54,642 --> 00:00:56,548
- Back to you!
- That really touched me!

21
00:00:57,688 --> 00:01:00,858
- Didn’t it?! I’m almost tearful!
- No, really.

22
00:01:00,883 --> 00:01:03,644
Thank you for your sacrifices and
for taking care of us and your mom –.

23
00:01:06,490 --> 00:01:07,316
- Why, why?!
- What’s going on?

24
00:01:07,341 --> 00:01:08,815
My love, what’s happening?!

25
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:10,766
- Dad! What’s wrong, Dad?
- Nothing, nothing. I’m fine, I’m fine!

26
00:01:10,790 --> 00:01:11,859
Hold on a second!

27
00:01:11,884 --> 00:01:13,157
- Yes?
- What about us?

28
00:01:13,594 --> 00:01:14,981
- What?
- It’s just you, huh?

29
00:01:15,006 --> 00:01:17,246
The sacrifices! My goodness, all
the sacrifices we’ve made for you!

30
00:01:17,270 --> 00:01:18,723
Why just me? Why is it always me?

31
00:01:18,748 --> 00:01:19,485
Kuya Aga!

32
00:01:19,510 --> 00:01:20,610
- Kuya Aga!
- Yeah?

33
00:01:20,892 --> 00:01:23,958
- There’s so many people outside!
- What’s with the plant you’re carrying?!

34
00:01:23,983 --> 00:01:27,439
I’m selling it since we have a lot of
plant enthusiasts among our guests!

35
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:29,736
Why do you look like that?

36
00:01:29,761 --> 00:01:33,668
Isn’t this our reopening – a grand
reopening, like a christening?

37
00:01:33,693 --> 00:01:34,101
Yes!

38
00:01:34,126 --> 00:01:36,292
That’s why I wore this – something playful!

39
00:01:36,317 --> 00:01:38,447
- Hold on…
- Let’s take this off!

40
00:01:39,722 --> 00:01:44,594
Wait a second. Maybe they
won’t get what we’re saying!

41
00:01:44,619 --> 00:01:45,828
- Them!
- Them!

42
00:01:46,138 --> 00:01:47,257
I know, them!

43
00:01:47,361 --> 00:01:48,361
- Who else?!
- You!

44
00:01:48,730 --> 00:01:55,779
Them. Here they are, you’ll
witness it, watch our amazing story.

45
00:02:58,412 --> 00:02:59,932
Oh, I’ll give you the change tomorrow!

46
00:03:02,404 --> 00:03:04,211
Here, here, here, press on it a bit.

47
00:03:10,438 --> 00:03:11,071
Kuya Aga…

48
00:03:11,096 --> 00:03:12,216
- Boss – Boss Beauty!
- What?

49
00:03:12,550 --> 00:03:15,237
I was just wondering
if I could buy…five kilos.

50
00:03:15,674 --> 00:03:17,747
Oh, sure, sure, sure, Kuya Aga.
He wants five kilos.

51
00:03:17,772 --> 00:03:18,772
Five kilos?

52
00:03:19,145 --> 00:03:19,991
Of rice, rice.

53
00:03:20,016 --> 00:03:21,300
Ah, five kilos too, Tso K?

54
00:03:21,437 --> 00:03:23,823
Five…? What five kilos?

55
00:03:24,190 --> 00:03:25,483
What do you take me for, retail?

56
00:03:25,950 --> 00:03:28,755
Are you comparing me to BFF? What, poor?!

57
00:03:29,546 --> 00:03:31,733
What five kilos – five sacks!

58
00:03:31,758 --> 00:03:33,023
Five sacks?! Oh, five sacks!

59
00:03:33,054 --> 00:03:34,722
Five sacks, get it from the storage!

60
00:03:34,747 --> 00:03:35,300
Hurry up!

61
00:03:35,325 --> 00:03:37,710
- Wait a minute, Tso K, okay?
- That’s five, five, five. Five sacks.

62
00:03:37,734 --> 00:03:40,401
- Oh, wait. Five sacks, five sacks!
- Wow, do you really need that much?

63
00:03:40,425 --> 00:03:42,791
When I buy five sacks, am
I oppressing people now?

64
00:03:43,484 --> 00:03:44,370
Of course. BFF, oh.

65
00:03:44,395 --> 00:03:45,673
- BFF, what can I do –?
- Hey, councilor!

66
00:03:45,697 --> 00:03:47,390
- Friends, neighbors!
- Councilor!

67
00:03:47,415 --> 00:03:49,089
- Constituents, friends!
- Hey!

68
00:03:49,521 --> 00:03:54,048
I just want to announce that we’ll
have a mass christening in two weeks!

69
00:03:55,740 --> 00:03:56,993
Mass christening?

70
00:03:57,463 --> 00:04:02,289
So if you have kids you want
baptized for free, just sign up!

71
00:04:02,609 --> 00:04:05,896
Hey, hey, Tso K! Let’s sign up!

72
00:04:06,486 --> 00:04:08,779
Why would we sign up?
Do we even have kids?!

73
00:04:08,834 --> 00:04:11,387
Not…yet!

74
00:04:11,412 --> 00:04:14,459
- Oh no!
- Tso K!

75
00:04:14,484 --> 00:04:18,010
Mariposa, please! Keep
your distance, please!

76
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:20,626
I might not be able to
control myself, please!

77
00:04:20,651 --> 00:04:23,363
Mmm, calm down. BFF, just relax!

78
00:04:24,187 --> 00:04:25,079
Uh…what?

79
00:04:25,104 --> 00:04:27,638
Well, they won’t stop!

80
00:04:29,481 --> 00:04:31,134
Councilor! Sorry, sorry,
what were you saying again?

81
00:04:31,158 --> 00:04:34,060
Wait, wait…have you
already chosen godparents?

82
00:04:34,131 --> 00:04:35,238
Not yet, not yet!

83
00:04:35,263 --> 00:04:37,586
Include them too and have them sign up.

84
00:04:37,611 --> 00:04:38,432
- Picking who?
- Kuya Aga!

85
00:04:38,457 --> 00:04:40,220
- Not me, not me!
- Kuya Aga, Kuya Aga!

86
00:04:40,921 --> 00:04:41,780
Not me!

87
00:04:41,817 --> 00:04:44,201
- Tso K, Tso K, Tso K!
- Not me, not me!

88
00:04:44,779 --> 00:04:45,779
Not me!

89
00:04:47,474 --> 00:04:48,994
You’re going to break me in half!

90
00:04:49,027 --> 00:04:50,027
My Tso K!

91
00:04:51,223 --> 00:04:54,670
What do you mean godfather
– I don’t even want to be one!

92
00:04:54,695 --> 00:04:55,891
We want you!

93
00:04:55,916 --> 00:04:57,507
Why did you ripped my shirt?!

94
00:04:57,642 --> 00:04:59,208
That's what I'm telling you.

95
00:04:59,233 --> 00:05:01,066
Because you are contradicting!

96
00:05:01,091 --> 00:05:02,996
Look at me. I'm okay, right?

97
00:05:03,021 --> 00:05:04,021
See?

98
00:05:07,208 --> 00:05:07,828
Hello!

99
00:05:08,114 --> 00:05:09,114
Here.

100
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:12,573
Here’s your order!

101
00:05:13,324 --> 00:05:15,084
Enjoy, enjoy!
Here’s this one too!

102
00:05:15,347 --> 00:05:16,961
This is totally your fault!

103
00:05:17,215 --> 00:05:22,320
You, Aga! You’re my BFF,
but this is all your doing!

104
00:05:22,452 --> 00:05:24,165
Why is this my fault?

105
00:05:24,190 --> 00:05:25,279
Why?!

106
00:05:25,304 --> 00:05:28,288
Look what happened to my
shirt, it turned into a tank top!

107
00:05:28,405 --> 00:05:30,901
Well, they’re looking for godparents,
and you don’t want to do it?

108
00:05:30,925 --> 00:05:33,718
Hey, hey, what’s going
on?! You two are so loud!

109
00:05:33,787 --> 00:05:34,553
Exactly!

110
00:05:34,578 --> 00:05:37,318
You two best friends are
arguing again, what’s going on?!

111
00:05:37,343 --> 00:05:39,218
It’s simple.

112
00:05:39,542 --> 00:05:45,442
This guy is being invited to be a
godfather for the mass christening.

113
00:05:45,467 --> 00:05:45,970
Oh?

114
00:05:46,283 --> 00:05:47,196
And he doesn’t want to!

115
00:05:47,228 --> 00:05:47,949
- What?!
- What?!

116
00:05:47,974 --> 00:05:49,203
- He’s refusing!
- Oh, why?!

117
00:05:49,228 --> 00:05:49,664
Why?

118
00:05:50,108 --> 00:05:51,588
I’m really refusing!

119
00:05:51,613 --> 00:05:52,181
Oh? Look at that.

120
00:05:52,206 --> 00:05:54,460
Well, I know they’re
only asking me to be a

121
00:05:54,484 --> 00:05:57,170
godfather because they
know I’ll give a big gift!

122
00:05:57,375 --> 00:05:59,062
Oh, look at the state I’m in now!

123
00:05:59,519 --> 00:06:00,585
Oh my, you.

124
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:02,788
Don’t you know there’s
a saying that if you

125
00:06:02,812 --> 00:06:05,355
refuse to be a godparent,
you’ll have bad luck!

126
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:05,763
Mmm!

127
00:06:05,788 --> 00:06:06,948
Oh? That’s true?!

128
00:06:06,973 --> 00:06:08,068
- Yes!
- Yes!

129
00:06:08,287 --> 00:06:09,960
Between us, who has debts?

130
00:06:10,298 --> 00:06:10,978
- We do!
- We do!

131
00:06:11,215 --> 00:06:12,215
Who are you indebted to?!

132
00:06:12,426 --> 00:06:13,400
- You!
- You!

133
00:06:13,437 --> 00:06:14,690
Now who’s the unlucky one?

134
00:06:15,081 --> 00:06:15,695
- We are!
- We are!

135
00:06:15,814 --> 00:06:16,334
Oh.

136
00:06:16,365 --> 00:06:20,526
Then you’re the unlucky ones!
So that saying isn’t true, Lola Maxi.

137
00:06:21,140 --> 00:06:22,286
How did that happen?

138
00:06:25,163 --> 00:06:26,283
Uh…can I ask something?

139
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:28,813
Uh, do you know anyone named Jennifer?

140
00:06:30,193 --> 00:06:31,259
- No.
- Nope?

141
00:06:31,619 --> 00:06:32,625
- Yeah.
- Brad, you?

142
00:06:32,725 --> 00:06:33,885
Do you know a Jennifer?

143
00:06:34,385 --> 00:06:34,765
Nope.

144
00:06:34,790 --> 00:06:35,790
Nope?

145
00:06:37,030 --> 00:06:38,030
Boss, excuse me!

146
00:06:38,703 --> 00:06:39,243
- Yes?
- Yes?

147
00:06:39,268 --> 00:06:40,878
Uh, do you know anyone named Jennifer?

148
00:06:41,322 --> 00:06:42,542
- Jennifer?
- Jennifer.

149
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:44,120
- Nope.
- Oh, nope?

150
00:06:44,566 --> 00:06:46,313
How about you, Ma’am? Sir?

151
00:06:46,930 --> 00:06:47,810
- Jennifer?
- Jennifer.

152
00:06:47,835 --> 00:06:48,283
Nope.

153
00:06:48,463 --> 00:06:49,029
- Nope.
- Nope either?

154
00:06:49,054 --> 00:06:50,567
Do you know a Jennifer?

155
00:06:50,893 --> 00:06:51,893
I do!

156
00:06:52,233 --> 00:06:54,913
But I can’t find her,
that’s why I’m asking.

157
00:06:54,938 --> 00:06:56,018
What does she look like?

158
00:06:56,222 --> 00:06:59,688
Uh, I don’t have a picture,
but she’s kind of tall.

159
00:07:00,068 --> 00:07:00,688
- Mm-hmm?
- Okay?

160
00:07:00,713 --> 00:07:03,947
And her nose, well…it’s really…really wide.

161
00:07:04,007 --> 00:07:05,007
Is this guy joking?

162
00:07:05,266 --> 00:07:06,480
Like he’s saying –.

163
00:07:06,608 --> 00:07:07,877
No! She just kind of looks like you!

164
00:07:07,901 --> 00:07:09,355
Are you sure the one
you’re looking for is Jennifer?

165
00:07:09,379 --> 00:07:10,767
What is this, a security guard?

166
00:07:10,792 --> 00:07:13,027
But…she’s ugly.
She’s ugly, really.

167
00:07:13,313 --> 00:07:14,760
- I’m ugly?!
- Yes, yes.

168
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:21,073
Jennifer!

169
00:07:28,219 --> 00:07:30,819
- Is there something still in the oven?
- Yes, there is, there is.

170
00:07:32,097 --> 00:07:34,850
- What’s going on?!
- Jennifer, come on!

171
00:07:34,875 --> 00:07:38,253
Ispikerspine, I’m not Jennifer!
Stop calling me Jennifer!

172
00:07:38,340 --> 00:07:41,593
Jennifer, stop pretending. You’re Jennifer!

173
00:07:41,632 --> 00:07:42,675
Let’s make up!

174
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:45,972
I’m not Jennifer! My name is Iskineport!

175
00:07:46,025 --> 00:07:48,112
Why are you even here?
What are you doing here?!

176
00:07:48,167 --> 00:07:50,267
My contract’s over, right?

177
00:07:50,403 --> 00:07:52,123
That’s why I came to get you.

178
00:07:52,148 --> 00:07:56,227
I need two tattoo
artists to go to America!

179
00:07:56,285 --> 00:07:59,323
Come with me, Jennifer,
so we can fulfill our dreams!

180
00:07:59,348 --> 00:07:59,943
I don’t want to!

181
00:07:59,968 --> 00:08:03,323
Hey, are you Jennifer?

182
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:05,500
No! I’m Iski–Iskineport.

183
00:08:05,525 --> 00:08:07,425
- Huh?
- She’s Jennifer!

184
00:08:07,450 --> 00:08:10,186
- Jennifer?!
- Her real name is Jennifer!

185
00:08:10,350 --> 00:08:11,796
We grew up together!

186
00:08:12,047 --> 00:08:12,567
Huh?!

187
00:08:12,599 --> 00:08:15,484
Her mom’s name is Jenny!

188
00:08:17,632 --> 00:08:19,205
Jenny? And then?

189
00:08:19,536 --> 00:08:22,343
And her dad’s name is Ferdie!

190
00:08:22,368 --> 00:08:22,729
And?

191
00:08:22,754 --> 00:08:26,377
So they combined their
names, and her name is Jennifer!

192
00:08:26,402 --> 00:08:27,323
- Hey!
- Wait a second!

193
00:08:27,348 --> 00:08:30,035
Iskineport, is that true?!

194
00:08:30,297 --> 00:08:34,230
No, Ate Cha! My real name is Iskineport.

195
00:08:34,293 --> 00:08:37,180
You’re exposing me here!
Aren’t you supposed to be abroad?!

196
00:08:37,205 --> 00:08:40,365
That’s why I came back—to take you with me!

197
00:08:40,390 --> 00:08:42,005
There’s a new opportunity.

198
00:08:42,042 --> 00:08:44,659
They need two tattoo artists in America!

199
00:08:45,293 --> 00:08:46,333
Come on!

200
00:08:46,358 --> 00:08:47,143
No way!

201
00:08:47,345 --> 00:08:50,716
Even if I barely get
paid here by Kuya Aga,

202
00:08:50,740 --> 00:08:54,112
or don’t get paid at
all, money can’t buy me!

203
00:08:54,137 --> 00:08:55,099
I’m not going with you!

204
00:08:55,130 --> 00:08:57,240
Hold on! You’re getting mad again!

205
00:08:57,265 --> 00:08:57,813
Kuya Aga, I love you!

206
00:08:57,838 --> 00:08:58,838
Easy there, Eport!

207
00:08:58,904 --> 00:09:00,250
Easy there, Eport!

208
00:09:00,673 --> 00:09:01,679
Easy there?

209
00:09:01,952 --> 00:09:04,285
Easy there? Iski…neport?

210
00:09:04,332 --> 00:09:05,118
That’s it!

211
00:09:05,143 --> 00:09:06,729
That’s what Iskineport means?

212
00:09:06,754 --> 00:09:07,794
That’s where it came from!

213
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:10,426
I’m the one who gave
her that nickname back

214
00:09:10,450 --> 00:09:13,022
then because she always
had such a hot temper!

215
00:09:13,164 --> 00:09:16,818
I’d always say to her,
“Easy there, Eport!”

216
00:09:16,983 --> 00:09:20,650
Hold on, Kuya Ispikerspine,
where did your name come from?

217
00:09:20,737 --> 00:09:22,384
That’s my real name, Ispiker–.

218
00:09:22,409 --> 00:09:25,538
No! His real name is Kingkampum!

219
00:09:25,789 --> 00:09:26,569
Kingkampum?!

220
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:29,665
Hey, stop it! You’re making things up!
Come with me!

221
00:09:29,690 --> 00:09:32,928
I said I’m not going with you!
I’m not leaving Kuya Aga!

222
00:09:33,129 --> 00:09:34,915
Why not?! You’re wasting an opportunity...

223
00:09:34,940 --> 00:09:37,378
it’s a hundred thousand
a month, Jennifer!

224
00:09:38,077 --> 00:09:39,330
- Really?!
- Really!

225
00:09:39,452 --> 00:09:41,538
Kuya…a hundred thousand?

226
00:09:43,891 --> 00:09:44,891
Hey!

227
00:09:45,390 --> 00:09:48,324
We’re leaving. I don’t need you!

228
00:09:48,443 --> 00:09:49,869
I hate you! Let’s go.

229
00:09:50,282 --> 00:09:51,522
Fine, bye!

230
00:09:51,547 --> 00:09:52,593
- Wait a second!
- Tito!

231
00:09:52,952 --> 00:09:55,819
- It’s like…
- Iskinep–you have bread in the oven!

232
00:09:56,318 --> 00:09:57,152
He just left like that?!

233
00:09:57,177 --> 00:09:58,911
Unbelievable!
He threw something at me, did you see?!

234
00:09:58,935 --> 00:09:59,782
Yeah, I did!

235
00:09:59,862 --> 00:10:01,462
For a hundred thousand pesos!

236
00:10:01,487 --> 00:10:02,487
Are you hurt?

237
00:10:04,176 --> 00:10:04,783
A little.

238
00:10:04,808 --> 00:10:07,778
- A little?
- Yeah, a little! Here, here!

239
00:10:07,848 --> 00:10:11,847
But Dad, it seems like Tito
is a bit of a money-grabber.

240
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:13,640
Just a bit.

241
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,187
Like your Tagalog.

242
00:10:15,642 --> 00:10:16,642
Hey!

243
00:10:16,672 --> 00:10:19,779
- Wow! That hurt a bit!
- Oh, don’t be like that!

244
00:10:19,804 --> 00:10:21,733
Look at these two talking!

245
00:10:22,435 --> 00:10:24,508
Alright, then we’ll put this here.

246
00:10:31,956 --> 00:10:33,217
Nice.

247
00:10:33,754 --> 00:10:34,754
Looks good.

248
00:10:35,653 --> 00:10:38,846
Then this, it’s already filled.

249
00:10:38,932 --> 00:10:41,119
Wow, BFF!

250
00:10:41,907 --> 00:10:43,167
Lots of cash, huh?!

251
00:10:44,086 --> 00:10:45,533
Yeah! BFF!

252
00:10:45,793 --> 00:10:46,199
Hey!

253
00:10:46,296 --> 00:10:48,736
You just pop up out of nowhere
now, huh? You don’t even knock!

254
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:50,980
Hi, Karl!

255
00:10:51,070 --> 00:10:53,603
- It’s okay, no worries.
- I’m used to it…

256
00:10:53,628 --> 00:10:56,165
It’s just the money I’m setting
aside for my godchildren.

257
00:10:56,551 --> 00:11:00,061
Wow, you’re so excited—it’s
still two weeks away!

258
00:11:00,483 --> 00:11:05,720
Well, I’m setting it aside now.
You never know, I might spend it.

259
00:11:05,747 --> 00:11:06,747
I might end up using it.

260
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,100
- My love…
- Just to be safe.

261
00:11:08,665 --> 00:11:10,412
Take it easy.

262
00:11:10,437 --> 00:11:14,135
Don’t we still have to make payments
to Karl? You’re being too generous!

263
00:11:14,193 --> 00:11:15,193
See?

264
00:11:15,732 --> 00:11:18,579
Your wife is smart!

265
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:21,780
That’s why I love her!

266
00:11:22,164 --> 00:11:25,404
Oh, come on! Aren’t you used to it?

267
00:11:25,989 --> 00:11:30,515
Of course, his pride kicks in.

268
00:11:30,563 --> 00:11:35,536
He’ll pay so that
people think he’s loaded.

269
00:11:36,330 --> 00:11:38,550
Lola Maxi, it’s not like that.

270
00:11:39,098 --> 00:11:42,638
You know the Pers family
is known for being generous.

271
00:11:43,042 --> 00:11:49,175
And this money, it’s just a token for the
godchildren—a small way to guide them.

272
00:11:49,615 --> 00:11:54,785
And think about how
happy it’ll make their parents.

273
00:11:55,182 --> 00:12:01,198
Money can be earned, even if it’s
hard. It’s hard, but you can earn it.

274
00:12:01,631 --> 00:12:06,546
But the joy, guidance,
and help you give to them?

275
00:12:06,986 --> 00:12:08,592
That’s priceless.

276
00:12:09,285 --> 00:12:10,925
- You do have a point.
- Don’t I?!

277
00:12:10,990 --> 00:12:13,910
But we’re just reminding you.

278
00:12:14,083 --> 00:12:14,871
Mmm.

279
00:12:14,896 --> 00:12:16,363
Oh, no problem there.

280
00:12:16,394 --> 00:12:20,947
BFF will understand if I’m two
weeks late paying him. Right?

281
00:12:20,972 --> 00:12:22,639
Of course! But–.

282
00:12:22,664 --> 00:12:25,369
Hold on, what do you mean
two weeks?! I can’t allow that!

283
00:12:25,709 --> 00:12:28,882
What do you mean not
allowed? We’re giving gifts, right?

284
00:12:28,907 --> 00:12:30,819
Anyway, I have to go.

285
00:12:30,844 --> 00:12:31,911
- Wait a second!
- Let me handle this.

286
00:12:31,935 --> 00:12:33,676
Wait, there you go again!

287
00:12:33,701 --> 00:12:34,908
- Why?
- BFF!

288
00:12:34,933 --> 00:12:39,673
Wait! You’re agreeing to be the
godfather, and yet it’s at my expense?!

289
00:12:39,698 --> 00:12:41,191
No sacrifices!

290
00:12:41,216 --> 00:12:43,162
- That’s so you!
- You are getting paid!

291
00:12:43,187 --> 00:12:45,401
- Wait! Don’t leave!
- You can handle it, BFF!

292
00:12:45,426 --> 00:12:47,647
- BFF!
- Two weeks, two weeks! Two weeks!

293
00:12:47,672 --> 00:12:48,903
What?! Hey!

294
00:12:48,928 --> 00:12:49,622
Two weeks!

295
00:12:49,647 --> 00:12:51,359
Are you sure your
birth certificate is here?

296
00:12:51,383 --> 00:12:54,170
It’s not. I left it here,
but I can’t find it now.

297
00:12:54,431 --> 00:12:56,398
This looks like it’s all trash, honestly.

298
00:12:56,423 --> 00:12:58,736
Are you sure you even
have a birth certificate?

299
00:12:58,760 --> 00:13:00,965
Maybe you weren’t
registered, Jennifer!

300
00:13:02,689 --> 00:13:03,989
Hey, I was registered!

301
00:13:04,569 --> 00:13:05,649
You were really registered?

302
00:13:05,856 --> 00:13:06,790
Yes.

303
00:13:06,815 --> 00:13:08,495
You know what, Tito? Don’t worry about it.

304
00:13:08,617 --> 00:13:11,478
- I ordered your birth certificate online.
- There you go!

305
00:13:11,503 --> 00:13:13,833
Really? I’m grateful for you, Tash!

306
00:13:13,935 --> 00:13:14,468
Don’t worry.

307
00:13:14,493 --> 00:13:16,492
And you? You’re just
saying nonsense over there!

308
00:13:16,517 --> 00:13:17,363
Jennifer!

309
00:13:17,388 --> 00:13:18,388
Jennifer Dimaapi?

310
00:13:18,651 --> 00:13:20,184
Jennifer?! Oh, there she is! Jennifer!

311
00:13:20,209 --> 00:13:21,209
Jennifer!

312
00:13:21,608 --> 00:13:23,841
What? Jennifer is your name?

313
00:13:23,879 --> 00:13:24,911
- Mm-hmm.
- Yeah, that’s her.

314
00:13:24,935 --> 00:13:28,288
For such a big person,
and your name is Jennifer?

315
00:13:31,289 --> 00:13:32,874
- Get out of here.
- Easy now, easy there!

316
00:13:32,898 --> 00:13:35,028
Oh, come on! Can’t you
take a joke? Sign here!

317
00:13:35,864 --> 00:13:36,864
Easy, now!

318
00:13:37,686 --> 00:13:39,737
- You’re working me –
- Easy, Eport!

319
00:13:39,762 --> 00:13:43,453
- Your pen! Your pen, your pen!
- Easy there, Eport!

320
00:13:43,484 --> 00:13:45,410
- Stop it!
- Relax!

321
00:13:45,514 --> 00:13:46,748
There you go again!

322
00:13:46,773 --> 00:13:48,693
- Calm it down.
- You’re getting worked up again.

323
00:13:49,306 --> 00:13:51,559
Alright, open it up already and let’s see!

324
00:13:52,966 --> 00:13:53,966
Oh!

325
00:13:54,038 --> 00:13:55,038
No record?

326
00:13:55,206 --> 00:14:00,059
We are sorry, but we did not
see any match in our database.

327
00:14:00,657 --> 00:14:01,483
Nothing?

328
00:14:01,554 --> 00:14:02,787
I wasn’t registered?

329
00:14:05,166 --> 00:14:06,166
I told you so!

330
00:14:06,815 --> 00:14:07,948
I remember now!

331
00:14:08,314 --> 00:14:09,408
Good thing you remembered.

332
00:14:09,438 --> 00:14:13,201
Yeah! Your parents didn’t get you baptized!

333
00:14:13,226 --> 00:14:13,808
What?!

334
00:14:13,833 --> 00:14:15,837
- Isn’t that good news?
- I told you so!

335
00:14:15,862 --> 00:14:16,369
Right?

336
00:14:16,394 --> 00:14:17,834
- Why?
- Isn’t that good news?

337
00:14:17,859 --> 00:14:19,129
How is that good news?

338
00:14:19,372 --> 00:14:24,160
Okay, what Anne means is that
you can apply for late registration,

339
00:14:24,305 --> 00:14:25,551
so there’s still a solution.

340
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:26,578
There you go!

341
00:14:26,603 --> 00:14:30,465
And, Tito, you don’t have
to use the name Jennifer.

342
00:14:30,827 --> 00:14:31,107
That’s right!

343
00:14:31,132 --> 00:14:33,154
You can choose whatever name you want.

344
00:14:33,179 --> 00:14:34,043
That’s it!

345
00:14:34,070 --> 00:14:36,965
Um, since your parents are gone, right?

346
00:14:36,999 --> 00:14:39,332
- Mm?
- So it’s up to you now, Tito.

347
00:14:39,385 --> 00:14:41,231
So I can still use Iskineport?

348
00:14:41,291 --> 00:14:42,651
- Yes!
- You can!

349
00:14:42,676 --> 00:14:43,841
But, late registration?

350
00:14:43,866 --> 00:14:44,866
- Yes!
- Mmm!

351
00:14:58,201 --> 00:15:01,428
Okay, so I guess this is it!

352
00:15:02,798 --> 00:15:04,498
I'm leaving now, leaving you behind.

353
00:15:04,523 --> 00:15:05,781
Take care, okay?

354
00:15:06,475 --> 00:15:09,926
I hope one day you'll understand me.

355
00:15:11,503 --> 00:15:12,503
I'm off!

356
00:15:15,262 --> 00:15:16,262
Going ahead!

357
00:15:17,968 --> 00:15:19,054
Understand?

358
00:15:19,962 --> 00:15:21,353
We were supposed to do this together!

359
00:15:21,377 --> 00:15:24,383
I was the one who backed
out, and now you're leaving first!

360
00:15:25,833 --> 00:15:29,020
If you're not taking me with you,
I'll just stay here in the Philippines!

361
00:15:46,046 --> 00:15:47,046
Bro!

362
00:15:48,548 --> 00:15:49,548
Bro!

363
00:15:52,502 --> 00:15:53,162
You okay?

364
00:15:53,289 --> 00:15:55,049
I'm fine, why did you slap me?

365
00:15:55,074 --> 00:15:57,245
No, it's like... you were zoning out, bro!

366
00:15:57,270 --> 00:16:00,517
I found you just... lying here like this.

367
00:16:00,542 --> 00:16:04,974
Maybe you need help?
I can take you home!

368
00:16:05,857 --> 00:16:07,917
No, it's fine. I'll just stay here.

369
00:16:08,230 --> 00:16:09,230
Huh? Are you sure?

370
00:16:09,796 --> 00:16:10,796
I'm okay here.

371
00:16:11,333 --> 00:16:13,120
No, you seem like you need help.

372
00:16:13,145 --> 00:16:17,861
If you don’t have a place
to stay, you can stay with us.

373
00:16:18,021 --> 00:16:21,235
By the way, I'm Aga.

374
00:16:21,633 --> 00:16:22,633
Aga Pers.

375
00:16:23,099 --> 00:16:25,125
Uh, I'm...

376
00:16:26,792 --> 00:16:27,792
Who are you?

377
00:16:29,126 --> 00:16:30,153
Iskineport Do.

378
00:16:30,608 --> 00:16:31,868
Iskineport Do?

379
00:16:31,952 --> 00:16:32,952
Mm-mm.

380
00:16:33,974 --> 00:16:36,027
No way. Aren’t you Jennifer?

381
00:16:36,455 --> 00:16:38,661
Uh, my name’s Iskineport.

382
00:16:38,830 --> 00:16:40,783
No, you're Jennifer!

383
00:16:40,808 --> 00:16:42,398
- I’m—not Jennifer.
- You're Jennifer!

384
00:16:42,423 --> 00:16:43,438
I’m not Jennifer!

385
00:16:43,463 --> 00:16:45,082
- You're Jennifer!
- I’m not Jennifer!

386
00:16:45,107 --> 00:16:46,362
- You're Jennifer!
- I’m not Jennifer!

387
00:16:46,386 --> 00:16:48,667
- Jennifer! Jennifer! You’re Jennifer!
- I’m not Jennifer!

388
00:16:50,871 --> 00:16:51,211
Hey!

389
00:16:51,236 --> 00:16:52,884
- I’m not Jennifer!
- Hey, Iskineport!

390
00:16:52,909 --> 00:16:54,219
- I’m not Jennifer!
- Psst, hey!

391
00:16:55,183 --> 00:16:59,846
- Hey!
- Ouch! Iskineport, wake up!

392
00:17:00,679 --> 00:17:01,806
What’s wrong with you?!

393
00:17:02,085 --> 00:17:03,858
You were dreaming!

394
00:17:04,594 --> 00:17:05,594
Chard!

395
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:06,213
What?

396
00:17:06,238 --> 00:17:08,448
Are you getting back at me?
Why did you slap me?!

397
00:17:08,516 --> 00:17:12,613
It’s all that cold rice you’ve been eating,
that’s why you're having nightmares!

398
00:17:12,948 --> 00:17:15,362
Well, I fell asleep
because I was preparing...

399
00:17:15,387 --> 00:17:17,067
- And why did you sleep here?!
- Yeah, why?

400
00:17:17,185 --> 00:17:20,533
Why’d you sleep here when you
could’ve just gone to bed... right?!

401
00:17:21,237 --> 00:17:22,850
You know, I was about to explain that!

402
00:17:23,014 --> 00:17:24,502
You didn’t have to butt
in with another question!

403
00:17:24,526 --> 00:17:26,174
It’s making me
look like I’m at fault!

404
00:17:26,711 --> 00:17:32,405
I slept here because I wanted
to prepare the bread earlier!

405
00:17:32,745 --> 00:17:35,606
Because I’m getting a
new birth certificate, and so

406
00:17:35,631 --> 00:17:38,491
you’ll stop calling me
Jennifer—I’m changing my name.

407
00:17:38,516 --> 00:17:41,618
Exactly! Nailed it!

408
00:17:41,643 --> 00:17:43,693
I know someone from the census!

409
00:17:43,718 --> 00:17:45,979
You can get that sorted
right away, and you’ll

410
00:17:46,003 --> 00:17:47,846
have your birth
certificate in two weeks!

411
00:17:47,871 --> 00:17:48,871
Oh, great!

412
00:17:48,950 --> 00:17:52,937
Why are you shouting? You’re
acting all helpful, but this is your fault!

413
00:17:52,962 --> 00:17:53,319
Hey!

414
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:54,959
You exposed my name as Jennifer!

415
00:17:54,984 --> 00:17:57,267
- No—
- Now I have no choice but to change it!

416
00:17:57,292 --> 00:17:58,292
It’s not like that!

417
00:17:58,377 --> 00:18:00,323
- It’s Iskineport!
- You’re the one getting help here!

418
00:18:00,347 --> 00:18:04,601
Iskineport, why are you complaining?
Spickerspine’s helping you!

419
00:18:04,858 --> 00:18:05,191
Yeah!

420
00:18:05,216 --> 00:18:07,568
What’s up with your
names—Spickerspine, Iskineport?!

421
00:18:08,192 --> 00:18:09,639
I’m getting confused!

422
00:18:09,664 --> 00:18:12,078
See, you’re being helped,
yet you’re still complaining!

423
00:18:12,103 --> 00:18:13,144
Be grateful

424
00:18:13,481 --> 00:18:16,908
! At least now you can
finally fulfill your dreams!

425
00:18:18,289 --> 00:18:20,963
You’re right, Kuya.

426
00:18:21,409 --> 00:18:22,409
Thank you.

427
00:18:23,066 --> 00:18:27,904
I should get my birth certificate
sorted so we can leave earlier.

428
00:18:28,008 --> 00:18:33,814
It’s fine. I’m just really happy that
you’re slowly reaching your dreams.

429
00:18:33,839 --> 00:18:34,232
Mmm.

430
00:18:34,257 --> 00:18:35,405
- Go for it!
- Right!

431
00:18:35,430 --> 00:18:38,985
It’s all good with me. We’ll always
be here for you, remember that.

432
00:18:39,010 --> 00:18:41,250
I’ll go to bed early, and you
take care of things here, okay?

433
00:18:41,274 --> 00:18:43,973
Alright, alright, wait,
wait, wait, wait, wait!

434
00:18:44,073 --> 00:18:45,133
We’re heading home now!

435
00:18:45,163 --> 00:18:49,771
Exactly. Just
remember—your tattoo artistry.

436
00:18:49,887 --> 00:18:50,887
Of course.

437
00:18:51,264 --> 00:18:52,264
That’s it.

438
00:18:52,556 --> 00:18:55,996
This is the start of your
chance to improve your life.

439
00:18:56,021 --> 00:18:56,543
There!

440
00:18:56,756 --> 00:18:57,236
- Nice!
- Right?

441
00:18:57,769 --> 00:19:00,208
- No objections, it’s all for you.
- There!

442
00:19:01,055 --> 00:19:02,055
Thanks, Kuya.

443
00:19:02,203 --> 00:19:04,349
You know, I’ve always known you’re kind.

444
00:19:04,780 --> 00:19:08,160
That’s why I’ll really work hard abroad.

445
00:19:08,333 --> 00:19:08,713
Right.

446
00:19:08,775 --> 00:19:09,641
Let’s go, let’s go.

447
00:19:09,666 --> 00:19:11,485
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!

448
00:19:11,510 --> 00:19:12,510
What is it, Kuya?

449
00:19:12,642 --> 00:19:16,163
You know, sometimes,
opportunities like this are

450
00:19:16,226 --> 00:19:20,199
just stepping stones to
even bigger things for you.

451
00:19:20,628 --> 00:19:21,948
For us here, it’s no big deal!

452
00:19:21,973 --> 00:19:22,561
Don’t worry about it.

453
00:19:22,586 --> 00:19:25,896
Even if I’ll miss you,
and it’ll be hard without

454
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:29,230
you, just thinking about
your success in life…

455
00:19:29,255 --> 00:19:31,508
- Right.
- that’s it! Go on.

456
00:19:31,937 --> 00:19:32,937
Thanks, Kuya.

457
00:19:33,392 --> 00:19:35,072
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

458
00:19:35,131 --> 00:19:37,211
- No problem.
- Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!

459
00:19:37,988 --> 00:19:38,988
What is it, Kuya?

460
00:19:39,461 --> 00:19:40,608
Just remember, okay?

461
00:19:40,954 --> 00:19:41,594
I love you.

462
00:19:41,686 --> 00:19:44,586
Yes, you love me, I get it. I’m
not changing my name anymore.

463
00:19:45,326 --> 00:19:48,059
Neighbors! My name is Jennifer!

464
00:19:48,084 --> 00:19:48,868
- Oh, why—?!
- Captain!

465
00:19:48,893 --> 00:19:50,281
We’re not leaving anymore!

466
00:19:50,306 --> 00:19:51,124
Why aren’t you leaving?!

467
00:19:51,149 --> 00:19:54,004
This is my third attempt,
and you keep stopping me!

468
00:19:54,029 --> 00:19:55,736
I’m Jennifer!

469
00:19:55,976 --> 00:19:58,489
I’m not Iskineport, I’m Jennifer!

470
00:19:58,514 --> 00:20:01,424
Wow, amazing!

471
00:20:05,387 --> 00:20:05,913
So cool!

472
00:20:05,938 --> 00:20:09,033
Wow, impressive!
You’re really making sure

473
00:20:09,057 --> 00:20:12,529
tomorrow’s mass
christening will be perfect.

474
00:20:12,554 --> 00:20:16,505
Thank you, Ate Cha!
It’s fabulous, isn’t it?

475
00:20:16,530 --> 00:20:17,132
Super fabulous!

476
00:20:17,157 --> 00:20:21,679
That’s how we are here in Barangay
Singko—always helping each other!

477
00:20:21,733 --> 00:20:22,339
Correct!

478
00:20:22,364 --> 00:20:23,258
My love!

479
00:20:23,283 --> 00:20:26,103
Remember when we
baptized Andres and Atasha?

480
00:20:26,128 --> 00:20:27,610
- Mmm-hmm!
- Wasn’t it such a happy time?

481
00:20:27,634 --> 00:20:29,394
- It was so much fun!
- I just remembered it.

482
00:20:29,577 --> 00:20:32,243
That should’ve been me, but
someone else took her away.

483
00:20:33,274 --> 00:20:35,187
You’re talking to yourself again!

484
00:20:35,854 --> 00:20:36,327
What—?

485
00:20:36,417 --> 00:20:38,510
- You’re talking to yourself again!
- What I said?

486
00:20:38,561 --> 00:20:40,354
- Mmm-hmm!
- Yeah, it’s about you!

487
00:20:40,379 --> 00:20:41,134
What about me?

488
00:20:41,159 --> 00:20:43,020
Nothing, I just said I
hope you’ll be handsome

489
00:20:43,044 --> 00:20:44,822
tomorrow because
you’re a godfather!

490
00:20:44,847 --> 00:20:46,960
- Oh yeah, I’ll get ready!
- That’s what I said.

491
00:20:46,985 --> 00:20:47,709
You think it’s
something else again...

492
00:20:47,734 --> 00:20:49,308
Is that really what you
said? It sounded different!

493
00:20:49,332 --> 00:20:50,113
No, it’s the same!

494
00:20:50,138 --> 00:20:52,161
Hey! How are you all? Are you excited?

495
00:20:52,186 --> 00:20:52,999
- Yes, we are!
- Yes.

496
00:20:53,024 --> 00:20:53,586
We’ll ask for blessings!

497
00:20:53,617 --> 00:20:56,682
Of course! Hold on, hold on!
How many are you, in total?

498
00:20:56,753 --> 00:20:57,773
- Five.
- Five.

499
00:20:57,819 --> 00:21:00,033
Five? One, two, three,
four—there’s one missing?

500
00:21:00,337 --> 00:21:01,337
That’s okay!

501
00:21:01,407 --> 00:21:03,901
Perfect, I prepared five envelopes.

502
00:21:03,967 --> 00:21:05,727
I’ll take care of it. I’m so excited.

503
00:21:06,255 --> 00:21:08,275
- Look, they’ve grown so much!
- Kuya Aga!

504
00:21:08,522 --> 00:21:10,102
Hey, brother! How are you?

505
00:21:10,129 --> 00:21:12,049
Maybe you could also
be a godfather to our child?

506
00:21:12,566 --> 00:21:13,906
Um…

507
00:21:15,919 --> 00:21:17,366
yeah, sure, of course!

508
00:21:17,456 --> 00:21:19,056
It’s just that…

509
00:21:23,607 --> 00:21:28,064
I prepared envelopes for five
people exactly, so I’m a little short.

510
00:21:28,089 --> 00:21:31,794
But don’t worry, once I
save up again, it’s possible.

511
00:21:31,819 --> 00:21:34,336
Wow, Kuya Aga! I didn’t
know you were like this!

512
00:21:34,531 --> 00:21:35,931
You only help certain people!.

513
00:21:36,053 --> 00:21:37,999
Let’s go, let’s
find someone else!

514
00:21:39,021 --> 00:21:41,567
Wait, wait…uh. It’s not like that…

515
00:21:42,137 --> 00:21:44,491
it’s just... I’m really short on
money right now, you know?

516
00:21:44,516 --> 00:21:45,516
See, BFF?

517
00:21:46,212 --> 00:21:47,952
You don’t believe me.

518
00:21:48,109 --> 00:21:51,294
I told you, all they
want is your money.

519
00:21:51,995 --> 00:21:52,895
Wow, that’s harsh.

520
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:54,628
Yeah! Look, they’re so mad.

521
00:21:57,747 --> 00:21:58,720
- My love!
- My love.

522
00:21:58,744 --> 00:21:59,744
Yes?

523
00:21:59,997 --> 00:22:00,997
It’s okay.

524
00:22:01,512 --> 00:22:02,726
Mmm. It’s okay.

525
00:22:05,236 --> 00:22:07,489
I just don’t have
enough money. Right?

526
00:22:24,331 --> 00:22:25,331
This is hard.

527
00:22:27,251 --> 00:22:30,571
If only I were born rich, right?

528
00:22:31,430 --> 00:22:33,217
Imagine, if I were born rich,

529
00:22:34,501 --> 00:22:37,367
I could give
everything—everything to everyone.

530
00:22:39,468 --> 00:22:47,424
Just think, if I had money, if I was
blessed with these kinds of blessings,

531
00:22:47,810 --> 00:22:51,057
I’d share them all.

532
00:22:52,007 --> 00:22:53,447
I’d give them all away.

533
00:22:53,472 --> 00:22:54,912
What would I even do with all of it?

534
00:22:56,249 --> 00:23:01,002
My only happiness is making sure
my family eats three times a day.

535
00:23:01,313 --> 00:23:02,013
My love...

536
00:23:02,038 --> 00:23:04,198
But everyone else being
happy—that’s all I really want.

537
00:23:04,894 --> 00:23:08,060
- It’s okay, my love.
- It’s okay, Dad! Don’t worry about it!

538
00:23:09,415 --> 00:23:12,055
No, it’s just... you know,

539
00:23:12,936 --> 00:23:15,109
when you think about it,
I’m not selfish with money.

540
00:23:15,134 --> 00:23:15,796
Mm-hmm.

541
00:23:16,071 --> 00:23:20,471
If I have something, and if
I get more, I’ll give it away.

542
00:23:20,551 --> 00:23:24,786
I’d spend it all on people
who truly need it, right?

543
00:23:25,071 --> 00:23:25,884
Dad, you know...

544
00:23:25,971 --> 00:23:26,971
Mmm?

545
00:23:27,416 --> 00:23:30,176
You’re the most generous person we know.

546
00:23:30,342 --> 00:23:31,676
- Mmm.
- That’s true, Dad.

547
00:23:32,100 --> 00:23:33,016
It’s true.

548
00:23:33,041 --> 00:23:37,491
And whether you do something good or bad,

549
00:23:37,700 --> 00:23:40,835
people will always have
something to say about you.

550
00:23:42,514 --> 00:23:45,327
That’s why, Dad, don’t
let it bother you anymore.

551
00:23:45,873 --> 00:23:47,313
- It’s fine now.
- Thank you, Andres!

552
00:23:51,441 --> 00:23:54,441
You know, they’re right.

553
00:23:54,720 --> 00:23:55,720
Lola Maxi…

554
00:23:55,918 --> 00:24:01,444
So, forgive me for
what I said earlier, okay?

555
00:24:02,753 --> 00:24:06,703
Honestly, you’re not a prideful person.

556
00:24:07,334 --> 00:24:08,874
You’re a good person.

557
00:24:09,562 --> 00:24:12,415
Just ignore what others say.

558
00:24:12,440 --> 00:24:15,294
What matters is that
you know who you are.

559
00:24:16,417 --> 00:24:17,780
Is that true, Lola Maxi?

560
00:24:17,805 --> 00:24:18,805
Mmm!

561
00:24:18,924 --> 00:24:20,850
Could you... could you repeat that?

562
00:24:23,161 --> 00:24:24,308
I forgot what I said.

563
00:24:24,774 --> 00:24:26,081
What did I say again?

564
00:24:26,370 --> 00:24:28,576
You know... but really.

565
00:24:29,205 --> 00:24:31,372
How can you not be generous

566
00:24:32,141 --> 00:24:35,548
when you’ve been blessed
with this kind of family?

567
00:24:36,949 --> 00:24:39,332
- Wow!
- We love you!

568
00:24:39,357 --> 00:24:41,036
- I love you, too!
- I love you, Dad!

569
00:24:42,373 --> 00:24:43,373
Oh, hug, hug, hug!

570
00:24:44,266 --> 00:24:46,219
Group hug!

571
00:24:48,635 --> 00:24:50,282
Isn’t this nice?

572
00:24:50,788 --> 00:24:51,788
Eat up, everyone!

573
00:24:51,978 --> 00:24:55,972
Oh, there’s still more! This
is so good. Enjoy, enjoy!

574
00:24:56,241 --> 00:24:59,834
Yes, yes!

575
00:25:00,178 --> 00:25:03,091
Kuya! Ate Cha!

576
00:25:03,324 --> 00:25:05,244
Lola Maxi!

577
00:25:05,539 --> 00:25:08,726
I’m not Jennifer anymore!
I’m a new person now!

578
00:25:09,082 --> 00:25:13,608
My name is Iskineport! Iskineport Do!

579
00:25:14,965 --> 00:25:17,678
So... you’ve forgiven me, right?

580
00:25:18,668 --> 00:25:19,708
I forgive you.

581
00:25:19,733 --> 00:25:21,350
There!

582
00:25:21,375 --> 00:25:23,070
Right? You’re a new person now?

583
00:25:23,095 --> 00:25:23,570
Yes.

584
00:25:23,931 --> 00:25:25,678
So that means you
haven’t been baptized yet?

585
00:25:28,181 --> 00:25:28,995
Oh, right.

586
00:25:29,020 --> 00:25:30,020
Mm-hmm!

587
00:25:30,365 --> 00:25:33,185
You should join the
community baptism tomorrow!

588
00:25:34,006 --> 00:25:37,728
And don’t even think about
making me your godmother, okay?

589
00:25:38,765 --> 00:25:40,372
Wait, what?

590
00:25:40,705 --> 00:25:41,878
You’re getting baptized?

591
00:25:41,903 --> 00:25:42,903
Mm-hmm?

592
00:25:43,515 --> 00:25:45,228
My love, are you okay with that?

593
00:25:45,332 --> 00:25:46,079
Mmm!

594
00:25:46,120 --> 00:25:48,593
We’ll be your godparents—my love and I.

595
00:25:49,160 --> 00:25:50,240
- Oh!
- There you go!

596
00:25:50,486 --> 00:25:51,486
Oh, really?

597
00:25:51,526 --> 00:25:52,346
I don’t want that!

598
00:25:52,433 --> 00:25:53,093
Huh?!

599
00:25:53,367 --> 00:25:53,754
Yes.

600
00:25:53,861 --> 00:25:57,305
Uh, I don’t want you and
Ate Cha as my godparents.

601
00:25:57,330 --> 00:25:57,838
Wait...

602
00:25:57,863 --> 00:26:00,188
- So picky, huh?
- if not them, then who do you want?!

603
00:26:00,311 --> 00:26:03,591
It’s okay if they don’t want
to! No problem with me!

604
00:26:03,633 --> 00:26:05,606
Fine, the three of them!

605
00:26:06,031 --> 00:26:06,657
Huh?

606
00:26:06,682 --> 00:26:08,048
You, Andres, will be my godfather.

607
00:26:08,389 --> 00:26:11,016
Tasha, Anne, you’ll
be my godmothers.

608
00:26:11,041 --> 00:26:11,607
- Huh?
- Huh?

609
00:26:11,632 --> 00:26:12,606
For the baptism!

610
00:26:12,631 --> 00:26:13,137
- Us?!
- Us?!

611
00:26:13,162 --> 00:26:13,936
Yes!

612
00:26:13,961 --> 00:26:14,878
- Us?
- Yes.

613
00:26:15,321 --> 00:26:19,105
Wait, no offense, Uncle,
but... what does that mean?

614
00:26:19,559 --> 00:26:24,065
So, what should we call
you if we’re your godparents?

615
00:26:24,198 --> 00:26:25,198
Well...

616
00:26:26,373 --> 00:26:28,666
I know! Like Tso K!

617
00:26:29,106 --> 00:26:29,633
What’s that?

618
00:26:29,658 --> 00:26:31,743
So, "Tso," right?

619
00:26:31,768 --> 00:26:32,768
Yeah?

620
00:26:32,836 --> 00:26:34,463
- Godchild, child.
- Yes?

621
00:26:34,488 --> 00:26:38,750
Then, tiyo-nak! Tiyonak!

622
00:26:41,218 --> 00:26:44,843
It fits! You look like a tiyanak!

623
00:26:47,225 --> 00:26:48,398
Oh, tiyanak!

624
00:26:48,423 --> 00:26:50,780
Easy there, Eport! Easy!

625
00:26:50,805 --> 00:26:51,904
You! Don’t you dare...

626
00:26:54,021 --> 00:26:55,427
Iskineport!

627
00:26:58,213 --> 00:26:59,353
Did we see that already?

628
00:27:00,037 --> 00:27:02,117
- What about it?
- Oh, yeah, we’ve seen that already!

629
00:27:02,436 --> 00:27:05,113
There’s nothing there, though.
That’s the problem.

630
00:27:06,875 --> 00:27:08,828
I’m so tired from going around.

631
00:27:09,550 --> 00:27:10,550
What do we do?

632
00:27:10,800 --> 00:27:14,113
We still haven’t found
anything for Kuya Iskineport.

633
00:27:14,735 --> 00:27:15,675
Exactly.

634
00:27:15,700 --> 00:27:19,045
I didn’t think being a
godparent would be this tough.

635
00:27:20,061 --> 00:27:22,335
It’s so hard to
choose a gift, huh?

636
00:27:23,512 --> 00:27:24,418
That’s it.

637
00:27:24,443 --> 00:27:29,537
Even if we find something, the
problem is, it’s over our budget.

638
00:27:31,443 --> 00:27:32,836
I’ve got it! I have an idea!

639
00:27:32,896 --> 00:27:33,816
- Oh?
- Okay?

640
00:27:33,841 --> 00:27:34,841
- Okay.
- What is it?

641
00:27:35,028 --> 00:27:36,968
Just leave it to me! Don’t worry about it.

642
00:27:37,061 --> 00:27:38,075
- Okay! Okay, okay!
- You’re game?

643
00:27:38,099 --> 00:27:39,083
- You’re taking charge?
- You’re game, huh?

644
00:27:39,114 --> 00:27:40,221
- Yes! Game, go!
- No backing out!

645
00:27:40,245 --> 00:27:41,397
- Alright! Game, let’s do this!
- No backing out.

646
00:27:41,421 --> 00:27:41,856
Game?

647
00:27:41,881 --> 00:27:42,793
- Game! Game!
- Okay, game!

648
00:27:42,818 --> 00:27:43,818
- G!
- Okay.

649
00:27:43,959 --> 00:27:47,519
Da-da-di-da-da, da-da-di-do-do.

650
00:27:47,544 --> 00:27:48,544
We’re amazing!

651
00:27:49,545 --> 00:27:50,365
More energy!

652
00:27:50,390 --> 00:27:52,977
- Oh! Thank you!
- Thank you, Kuya!

653
00:27:53,002 --> 00:27:58,178
Oh, do you want this?! Here,
just like this! Oh, oh, lower!

654
00:27:58,216 --> 00:27:59,141
More energy!

655
00:27:59,166 --> 00:28:01,667
- Oh, thank you so much!
- Thank you, Kuya! You’re so kind!

656
00:28:01,692 --> 00:28:05,898
Thank you so much,
because... oh, oh, oh! Oh my god!

657
00:28:06,442 --> 00:28:07,442
Like this?

658
00:28:07,619 --> 00:28:10,629
For Tito Iskineport! For Tito Iskineport!

659
00:28:14,095 --> 00:28:15,935
Wow, we’ve got so much money now!

660
00:28:16,123 --> 00:28:19,129
Wow! Tash, you’re amazing!

661
00:28:19,154 --> 00:28:20,382
See what I told you?

662
00:28:20,828 --> 00:28:24,168
Just a little effort, and
we’ve earned it already!

663
00:28:24,193 --> 00:28:25,341
This is heavy, huh!

664
00:28:25,464 --> 00:28:28,504
See? We’re rich now! We
can buy a house and lot!

665
00:28:29,754 --> 00:28:33,729
Oh wait... by the way, where’s Orb?

666
00:28:34,036 --> 00:28:35,109
Where did he go?

667
00:28:40,278 --> 00:28:41,085
Oh!

668
00:28:41,138 --> 00:28:42,612
- Fifty pesos, miss?
- Wow, fifty pesos?!

669
00:28:42,636 --> 00:28:44,111
- Yes, miss!
- Amazing!

670
00:28:45,239 --> 00:28:46,239
Mwah!

671
00:28:46,918 --> 00:28:48,245
- Fifty pesos?
- Go!

672
00:28:48,571 --> 00:28:49,591
Okay!

673
00:28:49,922 --> 00:28:50,669
Mwah!

674
00:28:50,828 --> 00:28:52,175
Wow!

675
00:28:52,605 --> 00:28:53,605
Hey!

676
00:29:03,873 --> 00:29:04,873
Parents,

677
00:29:05,640 --> 00:29:07,466
godfathers, godmothers,

678
00:29:08,227 --> 00:29:11,540
what do you wish for the
children? For the adults?

679
00:29:12,882 --> 00:29:13,908
Baptism.

680
00:29:14,816 --> 00:29:18,669
Then, do you renounce Satan?

681
00:29:22,934 --> 00:29:25,074
Yes, we renounce him.

682
00:29:28,124 --> 00:29:29,124
Bog?!

683
00:29:31,022 --> 00:29:35,136
And do you also
renounce all his evil works?

684
00:29:39,161 --> 00:29:40,481
Why are you looking at me again?!

685
00:29:41,498 --> 00:29:44,663
Ah, yes! We renounce them.

686
00:29:44,688 --> 00:29:45,688
Yes!

687
00:30:02,472 --> 00:30:03,472
That’s a big one!

688
00:30:03,609 --> 00:30:05,469
Yes. It’s funny.

689
00:30:06,954 --> 00:30:11,411
Well, because… I’m big too,
Father, so the candle is big as well.

690
00:30:12,564 --> 00:30:19,096
May the godparents,
friends, and family be blessed.

691
00:30:19,651 --> 00:30:26,960
Keep them away from harm
and grant them abundant peace.

692
00:30:27,515 --> 00:30:28,729
- Amen!
- Amen!

693
00:30:30,170 --> 00:30:35,653
Go in peace, and may the
Almighty bless you. Amen.

694
00:30:35,678 --> 00:30:38,986
- Amen.
- Thank you, father!

695
00:30:39,011 --> 00:30:43,158
Yes! I’m baptized now! I’m baptized!

696
00:30:43,967 --> 00:30:47,287
So, how are you, ladies? All good?

697
00:30:47,333 --> 00:30:49,278
- All good!
- We’re doing great!

698
00:30:49,303 --> 00:30:50,882
The food’s really good, huh?

699
00:30:50,907 --> 00:30:52,317
Enjoy, everyone!

700
00:30:52,342 --> 00:30:53,342
Eat up, everyone!

701
00:30:54,202 --> 00:30:56,556
Look at that, huh! So good, right?

702
00:30:56,595 --> 00:30:58,469
- BFF...
- Yes, BFF?

703
00:30:58,550 --> 00:31:00,070
I just wanted to tell you something.

704
00:31:00,157 --> 00:31:01,157
What is it?

705
00:31:01,614 --> 00:31:03,734
It actually feels nice to be
a godfather at a baptism.

706
00:31:04,216 --> 00:31:05,409
It’s a good feeling.

707
00:31:06,579 --> 00:31:08,619
Yeah. It really is.

708
00:31:08,644 --> 00:31:11,244
It’s so heartwarming. You see how
many people you’ve made happy...

709
00:31:11,438 --> 00:31:15,546
And it feels great to share
your blessings with others, too.

710
00:31:15,643 --> 00:31:16,777
Oh, yes.

711
00:31:16,834 --> 00:31:21,510
So next time, don’t turn it down
when you’re asked to be a godparent.

712
00:31:21,817 --> 00:31:22,817
I won’t.

713
00:31:24,819 --> 00:31:25,365
Kuya Aga...

714
00:31:25,390 --> 00:31:26,954
Oh, oh! Wait... nothing!

715
00:31:27,495 --> 00:31:28,362
Anxious much?

716
00:31:28,387 --> 00:31:30,408
No, no, no... oh?

717
00:31:30,896 --> 00:31:34,776
I wanted to apologize
for how I acted yesterday.

718
00:31:35,631 --> 00:31:36,937
Father was right –

719
00:31:37,647 --> 00:31:42,707
being a godparent isn’t about
giving money or material things.

720
00:31:43,977 --> 00:31:48,730
It’s about being a good role
model and a second parent.

721
00:31:49,891 --> 00:31:51,251
And that’s what you are, Kuya Aga.

722
00:31:52,036 --> 00:31:56,083
So, if it’s okay with you, can
you still be my child’s godfather?

723
00:31:57,486 --> 00:32:01,763
Of course! Yes, of course, no problem!

724
00:32:02,120 --> 00:32:07,402
It’s just that, at first, I was really
struggling. But, thank you! Thank you.

725
00:32:07,927 --> 00:32:09,036
Have the baby ask blessings!

726
00:32:09,060 --> 00:32:12,627
Oh, sure! Blessings,
blessings from the godfather!

727
00:32:12,652 --> 00:32:14,579
Oh, wow!

728
00:32:14,665 --> 00:32:17,465
- Thank you so much, Kuya Aga!
- Oh, thank you so much, Pareng Jinggoy!

729
00:32:17,671 --> 00:32:18,371
Thank you!

730
00:32:18,396 --> 00:32:21,757
Thank you, thank you, thank you,
thank you! Thanks so much!

731
00:32:22,865 --> 00:32:23,939
Yes!

732
00:32:25,143 --> 00:32:26,143
Tito Eski…

733
00:32:26,647 --> 00:32:27,187
Here!

734
00:32:27,212 --> 00:32:28,216
- Wow!
- This is for you!

735
00:32:28,241 --> 00:32:29,241
Wow!

736
00:32:29,442 --> 00:32:31,282
You guys are amazing!

737
00:32:31,307 --> 00:32:31,955
This is for you.

738
00:32:32,085 --> 00:32:34,592
Thanks! I’m touched.

739
00:32:34,782 --> 00:32:38,135
This is the first time I’ve ever
gotten a gift from you guys.

740
00:32:38,160 --> 00:32:40,112
- It’s nothing, bro!
- No problem!

741
00:32:41,247 --> 00:32:42,247
Anytime!

742
00:32:42,500 --> 00:32:43,887
Thanks, you guys! Thank you!

743
00:32:45,233 --> 00:32:46,233
Iskineport...

744
00:32:46,360 --> 00:32:46,833
What?

745
00:32:47,230 --> 00:32:48,337
Why are you wearing that?

746
00:32:49,256 --> 00:32:54,670
Isn’t it tradition to dress the child in
white and put a veil after baptism?

747
00:32:54,695 --> 00:32:55,695
Wha–?!

748
00:32:55,845 --> 00:33:01,788
Oh, Iskineport, that outfit is only
for babies to keep them warm!

749
00:33:02,075 --> 00:33:03,148
Look at this guy!

750
00:33:04,578 --> 00:33:06,118
Oh, Iskineport!

751
00:33:06,143 --> 00:33:07,793
- What?
- I forgot to tell you!

752
00:33:07,869 --> 00:33:08,229
What?

753
00:33:08,254 --> 00:33:12,785
The person recruiting us was just
scamming us! They just took our money!

754
00:33:13,038 --> 00:33:13,532
Really?

755
00:33:13,557 --> 00:33:14,969
Yeah, sorry!

756
00:33:15,502 --> 00:33:18,175
So, all the effort I put
into this is wasted?

757
00:33:18,200 --> 00:33:18,628
Yeah...

758
00:33:18,823 --> 00:33:20,190
This is your fault!

759
00:33:20,840 --> 00:33:23,093
I’m sorry! Calm down, Eport!

760
00:33:27,625 --> 00:33:29,078
Enough already!

761
00:33:30,375 --> 00:33:31,309
Sorry!

762
00:33:31,334 --> 00:33:34,178
Wait, hold on, sorry about this, okay?

763
00:33:34,216 --> 00:33:35,490
Wait, wait, wait! Sssh!

764
00:33:35,515 --> 00:33:36,522
Alright, guys –

765
00:33:36,560 --> 00:33:43,436
in struggle and joy, Pers is first,
Pers is the hero! Eat Bulaga!

766
00:33:43,591 --> 00:33:49,509
Welcome to the grand
reopening of Bake Haus of U!

767
00:33:49,534 --> 00:33:51,669
This guy is so lucky! He has everything!

768
00:33:54,859 --> 00:33:55,859
What happened?

769
00:33:56,222 --> 00:33:58,429
Good morning, my love.

770
00:33:59,115 --> 00:34:00,569
What? I’m your dad?

771
00:34:00,715 --> 00:34:02,321
We’re adopted?!

772
00:34:02,346 --> 00:34:03,505
That’s impossible!

773
00:34:04,076 --> 00:34:05,530
We look so much alike!

774
00:34:05,693 --> 00:34:07,387
Aga and I switched lives!

775
00:34:07,470 --> 00:34:12,557
- Honeybunch!
- Yes? I’m here, honeybunch!

776
00:34:12,582 --> 00:34:15,255
I heard you’re having
problems with your family.

777
00:34:15,317 --> 00:34:16,605
There’s something going
on between you two?!

778
00:34:16,629 --> 00:34:17,768
Traitors!

779
00:34:17,793 --> 00:34:21,542
Don’t interfere with my business...

780
00:34:21,567 --> 00:34:24,410
Hep, hep, hooray! Just settle
it with a dance showdown!

781
00:34:24,435 --> 00:34:25,787
I don’t like those things!

782
00:34:26,267 --> 00:34:27,700
I don’t want any of that!
